  {
    "date": "2020-06-12",
    "term": "いつまでも",
    "kana": "いつまでも",
    "meaning": "forever, for good, eternally",
    "level": "N3",
    "pos": ["adverb (fukushi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["compound"],
    "headline": "Itsumademo is いつ (itsu, “when”) plus まで (made, “until, up to”) plus も (mo, “even, also”): literally “until even any time”.",
    "morphemes": [
      {
        "text": "いつ",
        "reading": "いつ",
        "meaning": "when"
      },
      {
        "text": "まで",
        "reading": "まで",
        "meaning": "until, up to"
      },
      {
        "text": "も",
        "reading": "も",
        "meaning": "even, also"
      }
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From いつ (itsu, “when”) + まで (made, “until, up to”) + も (mo, “even, also”, inclusive) Literally, \"until even any time\"."
      },
      {
        "quote": "The construction itsu made (\"until when\") is attested already as Old Japanese itu made in the Man'yōshū of 759 CE. Likewise, the construction made mo (\"even until\") is also attested in the Man'yōshū, as is itu mo (\"any time, whenever; always\"). That said, the earliest attestation of the full phrase itsu made mo might not be until the Shaku Nihongi in the late 1200s."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
